    "title": "Tyler manicure school has license revoked, facing $15,500 fine - NewsBreak",
    "text": "TYLER, Texas ( KETK ) – The Texas Department of Licensing and Regulation has fined a Tyler manicure school and revoked their license after a complaint alleged they didn’t keep student records. The American Manicure School of Art in Tyler has been ordered to pay a $15,500 administrative penalty after they reportedly didn’t keep a student’s documents for 48 months after their withdrawal or termination, according to the Texas Department of Licensing and Regulation (TDLR). The TDLR stated that the school lacked a refund policy for unused student payments, failed to report the number of hours earned, and did not comply with a prior departmental order. As a result of their findings, the TDLR said the school’s private school license was revoked. You can now stream KETK and FOX51 News live 24/7 on your smart TV with KETK+ , our brand-new app! No antenna, cable, or satellite needed— watch for free, anytime. Just download it on your Roku, Apple TV, or Fire TV and start streaming. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KETK.com | FOX51.com.",
